# Tropical Tools

tropicraft.encyclopedia.dagger.title=Dagger
tropicraft.encyclopedia.dagger.desc=Weilded by the Koa tribe when hunting or when attacked.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboospear.title=Bamboo Spear
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboospear.desc=This sharpened stick is extremely powerful when first crafted. Be warned though, the spear looses its sharpness quickly.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishingrod.title=Bamboo Fishing Rod
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishingrod.desc=A must have tool for any budding fisherman, this rod has a light weight feel and an ergonomic design that makes fishing for supper a breeze!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.waterwand.title=Water Wand
tropicraft.encyclopedia.waterwand.desc=This mysterious rod has the unique ability to absorb 1000 blocks of water. This property makes the Water Wand perfect for creating water free underwater abodes.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.portalstarter.title=Tropicraft Portal Enchanter
tropicraft.encyclopedia.portalstarter.desc=This item, made with enchanted azurite and zircon, forms a portal that can be used to teleport between the Tropics and overworld when right-clicked on a 3x3 flat square of sandstone filled with water inside.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishingnet.title=Fishing Net
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishingnet.desc=This sturdy net is great for picking up the small fish that inhabit the Tropics. Be sure to have a water bucket, or you won't have anywhere to place you fish.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishbucket.title=Fish in a Bucket
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fishbucket.desc=Use this to place the fish that you catch in the wild. Make an aquarium, perhaps!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.dart_gun.title=Dart Gun
tropicraft.encyclopedia.dart_gun.desc=This tube of bamboo is used to shoot neurotoxin-laced darts at your pray. You will be surprised how a far and fast you can shoot a dart with a hefty blow. Neurotoxins not included.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.hoesouzium.title=Souzium Aqua Hoe
tropicraft.encyclopedia.hoesouzium.desc=Hoe constructed of an unknown material that mines faster while underwater, but slower above water.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.pickaxesouzium.title=Souzium Aqua Pickaxe
tropicraft.encyclopedia.pickaxesouzium.desc=Pickaxe constructed of an unknown material that mines faster while underwater, but slower above water.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.shovelsouzium.title=Souzium Aqua Shovel
tropicraft.encyclopedia.shovelsouzium.desc=Shovel constructed of an unknown material that mines faster while underwater, but slower above water.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.axesouzium.title=Souzium Aqua Axe
tropicraft.encyclopedia.axesouzium.desc=Axe constructed of an unknown material that mines faster while underwater, but slower above water.

# Armors

tropicraft.encyclopedia.firehelm.title=Fire Helmet
tropicraft.encyclopedia.firehelm.desc=Helmet constructed of an unknown material that gains durability when in fire, but don't stand in the fire too long, or you will be burned!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.firechestplate.title=Fire Chestplate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.firechestplate.desc=Chestplate constructed of an unknown material that gains durability when in fire, but don't stand in the fire too long, or you will be burned!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fireleggings.title=Fire Leggings
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fireleggings.desc=Leggings constructed of an unknown material that gains durability when in fire, but don't stand in the fire too long, or you will be burned!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fireboots.title=Fire Boots
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fireboots.desc=Boots constructed of an unknown material that gains durability when in fire, but don't stand in the fire too long, or you will be burned!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scalehelm.title=Scale Helmet
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scalehelm.desc=Helmet made of iguana scales that provides fire resistance for whomever wears it.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scalechestplate.title=Scale Chestplate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scalechestplate.desc=Chestplate mesh of iguana scales that provides fire resistance for whomever wears it.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scaleleggings.title=Scale Leggings
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scaleleggings.desc=Leggings made of iguana scales that provide fire resistance for whomever wears them.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scaleboots.title=Scale Boots
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scaleboots.desc=Boots made out of iguana scales that provide fire resistance for whomever wears them.

# Scuba Gear

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubaflippers.title=Scuba Flippers
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubaflippers.desc=These flexible flippers come in two different colors: pink and yellow! You can glide around the tropics water effortlessly wearing these bad boys. Hint: Do a barrel roll!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubachestplate.title=Scuba Chestplate Gear
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubachestplate.desc=This complicated looking scuba chestplate allows you to wear a number of scuba tanks. Shift + right click the item to wear up to 2 scuba tanks!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubagoggles.title=Scuba Goggles
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubagoggles.desc=This piece of the scuba suit allows you to not only view the values from your Dive Computer, but breathe air from the scuba tanks you're wearing.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.divecomputer.title=Dive Computer
tropicraft.encyclopedia.divecomputer.desc=A rare piece of tropics technology, the dive computer logs various values from your time underwater. After you've swam for an hour, hand your dive computer to a Koa for a surprise!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.weightbelt.title=Weight Belt
tropicraft.encyclopedia.weightbelt.desc=The weight belt allows your scuba chestplate to keep you underwater.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.ponybottle.title=Pony Bottle
tropicraft.encyclopedia.ponybottle.desc=Always bring along a pony bottle on your long scuba dives. When you run out of air, a pony bottle will refill your air temporarily, allowing you to swim to the surface safely.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bcd.title=BCD
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bcd.desc=Short for "Buoyancy Compensator Device", the BCD helps get air from your tanks to your mouthpiece.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.regulator.title=Diving Regulator
tropicraft.encyclopedia.regulator.desc=This device regulates the pressure between the breathing gas and the diver. In other words, this thing helps you not go boom.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubatank.title=Scuba Tank
tropicraft.encyclopedia.scubatank.desc=Scuba tanks hold all the air that you breathe while diving. Refill your scuba tanks in an air compressor block.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.trimix.title=Trimix Gas Mixture
tropicraft.encyclopedia.trimix.desc=A breathing gas consisting of oxygen, helium, and nitrogen. Trimix can be placed in an air compressor to fill a tank with trimix-infused air, allowing the player to stay underwater for much longer!

# Beach Accessories

tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachchair.title=Beach Chair
tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachchair.desc=Ahhh. Cast your line into the warm blue ocean, watch as a school of fish slowly approaches, and do all of this in the luxury of a beach chair! Sit back and relax in a chair of one of sixteen colors.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachfloat.title=Beach Floats
tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachfloat.desc=These relaxing floats allow the gentle currents of the tropics to move you. They come in sixteen different colors.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachumbrella.title=Beach Umbrella
tropicraft.encyclopedia.beachumbrella.desc=A beach getaway is not complete until there is an umbrella to shade yourself with! Also comes in sixteen different colors.

# Tropical Flora

tropicraft.encyclopedia.reeds.title=Reeds
tropicraft.encyclopedia.reeds.desc=In the Tropics, sugar cane serves a new purpose: thatching.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo.title=Bamboo Shoot
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo.desc=Bamboo is by far the most versatile item in the Tropics. You can craft weapons, blocks, and mugs from this sustainable resource.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.coffeebean.title=Coffee Bean
tropicraft.encyclopedia.coffeebean.desc=The pit inside the red or purple fruit often referred to as a cherry. This is the seed for the coffee plants found throughout the tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.coral.title=Coral
tropicraft.encyclopedia.coral.desc=While these bioluminescent lifeforms are at home in the ocean, they are well suited for lighting up an aquarium.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.kapok.title=Kapok Leaves
tropicraft.encyclopedia.kapok.desc=These leaves are found on humongous trees that appear on rare occasions in rainforest biomes.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahogany.title=Mahogany Wood
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahogany.desc=This beautifully colored wood comprises all Tropicraft rainforest trees and make for a beautiful addition to any tropical paradise.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmwood.title=Palm Wood
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmwood.desc=Palm trees are made of a surprisingly sturdy wood. It can also be split into planks.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.lemonsapling.title=Lemon Sapling
tropicraft.encyclopedia.lemonsapling.desc=Grows into a lemon tree. When live gives you lemon saplings, make...lemon trees?

tropicraft.encyclopedia.limesapling.title=Lime Sapling
tropicraft.encyclopedia.limesapling.desc=Grows into a lime tree. Pucker your lips, limes are sure to leave a crazy aftertaste once you grow the lime sapling into a full tree!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.orangesapling.title=Orange Sapling
tropicraft.encyclopedia.orangesapling.desc=Plant this orange sapling, and soon you will have a fully-bloomed orange tree! Punch orange leaves, get orange. ??? Profit!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.grapefruitsapling.title=Grapefruit Sapling
tropicraft.encyclopedia.grapefruitsapling.desc=Grows into a grapefruit tree, where you can get yummy grapefruits from!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmsapling.title=Palm Saplings
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmsapling.desc=These shoots can only grow on sand. Like other trees, they grow best in wide open areas and benefit from the use of bone meal.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganysapling.title=Mahogany Saplings
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganysapling.desc=Grows into imposing tall trees with large leaf canopies.

# Decor

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmplanks.title=Palm Planks
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmplanks.desc=Palm planks come from palm wood which comes from palm trees!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmdoor.title=Palm Door
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmdoor.desc=A sturdy wooden door great for keeping the bad things out.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmfence.title=Palm Fence
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmfence.desc=Palm trees are made of a surprisingly sturdy wood. Its beautiful planks can create fences.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmfencegate.title=Palm Fence Gate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palmfencegate.desc=Palm trees are made of a surprisingly sturdy wood. Its beautiful planks can create fence gates.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.palm_trapdoor.title=Palm Trapdoor
tropicraft.encyclopedia.palm_trapdoor.desc=Don't mind this place holder text.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyplanks.title=Mahogany Planks
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyplanks.desc=Mahogany planks come from mahogany wood which comes from mahogany trees!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganydoor.title=Mahogany Door
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganydoor.desc=A sturdy wooden door great for keeping the bad things out.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyfence.title=Mahogany Fence
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyfence.desc=This beautifully colored wood comprises all Tropicraft rainforest trees and make for a beautiful addition to any tropical paradise.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyfencegate.title=Mahogany Fence Gate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahoganyfencegate.desc=This beautifully colored wood comprises all Tropicraft rainforest trees and make for a beautiful addition to any tropical paradise.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahogany_trapdoor.title=Mahogany Trapdoor
tropicraft.encyclopedia.mahogany_trapdoor.desc=Don't mind this place holder text.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bambooblock.title=Bamboo Block
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bambooblock.desc=This easy-to-craft block is made from sustainable bamboo. Watch out, it isn't very strong.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboochest.title=Bamboo Chest
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboochest.desc=A chest made out of bamboo! It will complete your tropical-themed shack!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboodoor.title=Bamboo Door
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboodoor.desc=This bamboo and thatch door is perfect for separating you from the wilderness. Be careful though, this door isn't very strong.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboofence.title=Bamboo Fence
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboofence.desc=This bamboo fence is great at keeping the bad things out. Careful though, this fence isn't very strong.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboofencegate.title=Bamboo Fence Gate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboofencegate.desc=This bamboo fence gate works fantastic with fences of all types. Like other bamboo blocks, it isn't very strong.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboostick.title=Bamboo Stick
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboostick.desc=A stick made of bamboo. Used in many tropical recipes to replace the use of sticks.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_ladder.title=Bamboo Ladder
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_ladder.desc=Clunk. Clunk. Clunk. Hear that? That's you, climbing up a ladder made out of bamboo.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_crafting_table.title=Bamboo Crafting Table
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_crafting_table.desc=The finishing touch for any tropical base of operation.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_trapdoor.title=Bamboo Trapdoor
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bamboo_trapdoor.desc=This bamboo and thatch trapdoor is perfect for separating you from the wilderness. Be careful though, this trapdoor isn't very strong.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.tropiframe.title=Bamboo Item Frame
tropicraft.encyclopedia.tropiframe.desc=This item frame functions the same way as a vanilla item frame but has a bamboo border.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkohead.title=Chunk O' Head
tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkohead.desc=The Easter Island Heads that can occasionally be seen are made up of this rock. It is a holy stone to those who built the Heads, and taking it is considered sacrilege.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkfence.title=Chunk O' Head Fence
tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkfence.desc=The Easter Island Heads that can occasionally be seen are made up of this rock. Surround your base with a lovely fence version of the block.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkfencegate.title=Chunk O' Head Fence Gate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.chunkfencegate.desc=The Easter Island Heads that can occasionally be seen are made up of this rock. This fence gate works wonderfully with all fence types.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.tikitorch.title=Tiki Torches
tropicraft.encyclopedia.tikitorch.desc=These tall torches are great for lighting up beaches.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchblock.title=Thatch Blocks
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchblock.desc=As easy to craft as it is to break, the thatch block provides another sustainable building material to Tropics. It can be crafted into stairs and slabs.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchdoor.title=Thatch Door
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchdoor.desc=As easy to craft as it is to break, the thatch block provides another sustainable building material to Tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchfence.title=Thatch Fence
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchfence.desc=As easy to craft as it is to break, the thatch block provides another sustainable building material to Tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchfencegate.title=Thatch Fence Gate
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatchfencegate.desc=As easy to craft as it is to break, the thatch block provides another sustainable building material to Tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatch_trapdoor.title=Thatch Trapdoor
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thatch_trapdoor.desc=This thatch trapdoor is perfect for separating you from the wilderness. Be careful though, this trapdoor isn't very strong.

# Flowers

tropicraft.encyclopedia.iris.title=Iris
tropicraft.encyclopedia.iris.desc=These tall purple flowers are quite a sight. They can easily be replanted.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.commelina_diffusa.title=Co. Diffusa
tropicraft.encyclopedia.commelina_diffusa.desc=Commelina Diffusa adds a pleasant blue to the landscape of the Tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.crocosmia.title=Crocosmia
tropicraft.encyclopedia.crocosmia.desc=These fiery little flowers are like miniature suns resting on the ground.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.orchid.title=Orchid
tropicraft.encyclopedia.orchid.desc=Orchids are perhaps the rarest of all the flowers in the Tropics. Their delicate pink and white petals are sure to add an air of sophistication to your home.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.canna.title=Canna
tropicraft.encyclopedia.canna.desc=This yellow-orange flower blends in well in the tropical realm, complementing the hard-hitting red of the red anthurium.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.anemone.title=Anemone
tropicraft.encyclopedia.anemone.desc=This bleach white flower adds a nice innocent, calm color to the realm.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.orange_anthurium.title=Anthurium, Orange
tropicraft.encyclopedia.orange_anthurium.desc=This strong orange colored flower has an red counterpart.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.red_anthurium.title=Anthurium, Red
tropicraft.encyclopedia.red_anthurium.desc=This strong red colored flower has an orange counterpart.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.magic_mushroom.title=Magic Mushroom
tropicraft.encyclopedia.magic_mushroom.desc=Found only in the rainforest, these mushrooms are mysterious, need to explore more.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.pathos.title=Pathos
tropicraft.encyclopedia.pathos.desc=Pathos, in greek, means 'an appeal to emotions'. This plant can only be found in rainforests.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.acai_vine.title=Acai Vine
tropicraft.encyclopedia.acai_vine.desc=Rotten branches that are growing from the ground that used to grow the acai fruit.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.croton.title=Croton
tropicraft.encyclopedia.croton.desc=Go ahead and try to figure out what color this is. I DARE you.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.dracaena.title=Dracaena
tropicraft.encyclopedia.dracaena.desc=This interesting peach and green colored plant can be found only in the rainforest.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fern.title=Fern
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fern.desc=Ferns can be found in rainforests throughout the realm.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.foliage.title=Foliage
tropicraft.encyclopedia.foliage.desc=Common greenery found in the tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.bromeliad.title=Bromeliad
tropicraft.encyclopedia.bromeliad.desc=This exotic red flower thrives in the thick of rainforests among the tree frogs and moist conditions.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.flowerpot.title=Bamboo Flower Pot
tropicraft.encyclopedia.flowerpot.desc=This flower pot can be used to beautify any garden by holding any tropical flower, plant, or sapling.

# Shells

tropicraft.encyclopedia.soloshell.title=Solonox Shell
tropicraft.encyclopedia.soloshell.desc=Named after the creator of Tropicraft's theme song "Trade Winds", the Solonox shell yields a chance of finding a black or white pearl inside, so be on the lookout!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.froxshell.title=Frox Conch
tropicraft.encyclopedia.froxshell.desc=Created to commemorate the donators of the yearly LoveTropics charity event.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.pabshell.title=Pab Shell
tropicraft.encyclopedia.pabshell.desc=Named after one of the original modders of tropicraft, Pablomittens, the Pab shell stands as one of the original items that was in tropicraft since v1.0, but was never given a use.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.rubeshell.title=Rube Nautilus
tropicraft.encyclopedia.rubeshell.desc=Named after one of the current modders of tropicraft, MrRube, the Rube Nautilus was actually made by MrRube before v1.0 of Tropicraft, but was never given a use...until now!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.starfishshell.title=Starfish Shell
tropicraft.encyclopedia.starfishshell.desc=A starfish-shaped shell that drops when you kill a starfish. Placeable on walls.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.turtleshell.title=Turtle Shell
tropicraft.encyclopedia.turtleshell.desc=This shell is great for sprucing up your beach bungalow.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.pearlb.title=Pearl, Black
tropicraft.encyclopedia.pearlb.desc=Has a very high trade value with the Koa tribe; found inside Frox conches on rare occasions.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.pearlw.title=Pearl, White
tropicraft.encyclopedia.pearlw.desc=Has a moderately high trade value with the Koa tribe; found inside Solonox shells.

# Tropical Music

tropicraft.encyclopedia.easternisles.title=Eastern Isles
tropicraft.encyclopedia.easternisles.desc=This awesome drum and bass track was produced by Frox. Kick back and enjoy.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.summering.title=Summering
tropicraft.encyclopedia.summering.desc=Downtempo summery vibes carefully crafted by Billy Christiansen. Pop a squat, craft a piña colada, and listen to this song to enhance your tropical relaxation experience.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.thetribe.title=The Tribe
tropicraft.encyclopedia.thetribe.desc=Upbeat tropical vibes brought to you by Emile van Krieken. Listen to this song while venturing through a Koa Village and you may find yourself a favorite among the villagers.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.tradewinds.title=Tradewinds
tropicraft.encyclopedia.tradewinds.desc=A chillout song produced by Frox. At 136 bpm, Trade winds is sure to help you relax during your tropical vacation.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.lowtide.title=Low Tide
tropicraft.encyclopedia.lowtide.desc=Produced by Punchaface, this chilled electronica track has a heavy bassline-driving melody and is sure to brighten any day in the tropics.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.buriedtreasure.title=Buried Treasure
tropicraft.encyclopedia.buriedtreasure.desc=Don't mind this place holder text.

# Miscellaneous

tropicraft.encyclopedia.nigel.title=Nigel Winthorpe
tropicraft.encyclopedia.nigel.desc=The person who's journal was used to write the Encyclopedia Tropica. He was the first to discover the Tropics after finding a strange staff in an unknown jungle temple. While his current were abouts are unknown one thing is certain, he sure won't needing this no more.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.coconutbomb.title=Coconut Bomb
tropicraft.encyclopedia.coconutbomb.desc=This explosive coconut is great for taking out anyone, or anything, that tries to get in your way.

#tropicraft.encyclopedia.curare.title=Curare
#tropicraft.encyclopedia.curare.desc=Mix various types of flowers together to make different types of curare, which can be used to make darts with all sorts of potion effects.

#tropicraft.encyclopedia.curarebowl.title=Curare Bowl
#tropicraft.encyclopedia.curarebowl.desc=Mix various types of flowers in this bowl to create different types of curare, which can be used to make darts with all sorts of potion effects.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.dart.title=Dart
tropicraft.encyclopedia.dart.desc=This neurotoxin-laced dart is capable of stopping most mobs in their tracks. Be careful though, the effect is only temporary. Darts can have varying potion effects associated with them. Now neurotoxin-free!

tropicraft.encyclopedia.fertilizer.title=Fertilizer
tropicraft.encyclopedia.fertilizer.desc=Fertilizer functions similar to bone meal, but also grows tropical flowers and fruit plants like pineapples.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.frogskin.title=Poison Frog Skin
tropicraft.encyclopedia.frogskin.desc=Poisonous tree frogs secrete a paralyzing toxin though their skin.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.iggyscale.title=Iguana Scale
tropicraft.encyclopedia.iggyscale.desc=The adorable iguanas that inhabit the tropics drop scales. What is unique about these scales is that they are fire retardant. Wearing armor made of scales will allow you venture into some pretty hot places.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.iguana_leather.title=Iguana Leather
tropicraft.encyclopedia.iguana_leather.desc=The adorable iguanas that inhabit the tropics also drop a green leather. This leather functions just like regular leather and can be used interchangeably. You can also make bongo drums with iguana leather!

#tropicraft.encyclopedia.koachest.title=Koa Chest
#tropicraft.encyclopedia.koachest.desc=A chest that spawns Koa. Use it to populate a village or bungalow!

#tropicraft.encyclopedia.leafball.title=Leaf Ball
#tropicraft.encyclopedia.leafball.desc=Leaf balls can only be obtained via a trade with a Koa tribe member. When you throw a leaf ball, as soon as it makes contact it disperses into many leaves.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.sifter.title=Sifter
tropicraft.encyclopedia.sifter.desc=Right click a sifter with a any kind of sand, wait about ten seconds, and out will pop up to three items. It could be rare shells, gold nuggets, or more!

#tropicraft.encyclopedia.snaretrap.title=Snare Trap
#tropicraft.encyclopedia.snaretrap.desc=This device is used for trapping mobs and players, rendering them immobile.

tropicraft.encyclopedia.section.tribes.title=Tribes
tropicraft.encyclopedia.section.mobs.land.title=Land Animals
tropicraft.encyclopedia.section.mobs.water.title=Under Da Sea
tropicraft.encyclopedia.ltinfo.title=What is Love Tropics?
tropicraft.encyclopedia.ltinfo.desc=Love Tropics is a yearly charity stream organized by Team Tropicraft to support tropical areas affected by natural disasters. Last year (2018), we raised over $35,000 for Team Rubicon!\n\nEach year, we put the name of everyone who donated in this book to be immortalized for their generosity. Join us next year for a great time with your favorite Mojangstas, streamers, YouTubers, and mod developers!\n\nGo to lovetropics.org for more info.
tropicraft.encyclopedia.lt18.title=Love Tropics 2018

